KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--winx64 --cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ the copy of a copy has the same message: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ destroyed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
no body for callee
--
The model of __std_exception_copy left the message null when its
allocation failed.  Symbolic execution then did not end on a copy of a
copy: the merge after the failed allocation's early return gives each
copied byte the value `malloc failed ? unknown : byte', and the loop that
finds the length of the copied message cannot resolve its condition.  The
copy is now taken to succeed, as [exception]/2 requires equal what()
strings of an exception and its copy.  The same unbounded loop made
cpp11_standard_stream_objects_initialized_msvc run out of memory with the
VS 2022 STL.
